SUPPLY CHAIN MORNING
Issue 318 | Tuesday, March 24, 2026

Good morning. We are an hour late today; a server in Virginia decided otherwise. Three stories and a number.

1) EU Cyber Resilience Act: reporting obligations for connected industrial software - what suppliers to EU plants must file from 2027
The European Commission published the implementing guidance for the Cyber Resilience Act's reporting regime yesterday. From September 2027, any vendor whose software or connected device is installed in a plant inside the EU must report actively exploited vulnerabilities to the ENISA single reporting platform within 24 hours of becoming aware, with a fuller notification at 72 hours and a final report within 14 days. The guidance confirms that this covers US vendors selling into EU manufacturing sites, including SaaS products with an on-premises agent or gateway. Products classified as "important" (the guidance lists industrial control software and plant-floor data collection among the examples) also need a third-party conformity assessment before the CE marking can be applied. Trade groups called the 24-hour window "unworkable for small vendors"; the Commission said the window is for notification, not for a fix. If you sell connected software into European plants, your 2027 roadmap just acquired a compliance line, and your customers' procurement teams will start asking about it well before then.

2) Central Valley cold-storage capacity tightens ahead of stone-fruit season
Public refrigerated warehouse occupancy in the Fresno-Visalia corridor hit 94% last week, the highest March reading on record, with the early stone-fruit season colliding with carryover almond and citrus inventory. Spot storage rates are up 20% on last year. Two new facilities totaling 450,000 square feet are under construction but do not open until 2027. Packers are trucking to Stockton and even Reno for space.

3) Port of Oakland March volumes
The port's preview puts March loaded imports up 6% year on year and exports up 9%, the best export month since 2022, helped by the early ag season and the new gate hours. Empties are down, which is the healthiest combination the port has reported in years.

NUMBER OF THE DAY: 24 hours. The Cyber Resilience Act's initial notification window, which is now the tightest security-reporting deadline in any major jurisdiction.

